{
  "rationale": "No race telemetry exists yet (iteration 0, no prior run), so this is a first-principles draft built on the contract. Speed: the course is about 4-5 m and must finish within 3 s, so the average must be at least about 1.5 m/s. I chose base_speed 1.5, which is fast enough to finish but leaves room for the curves, since leaving the track ends the run. Sensing: five sensors at 12 mm footprint, spaced 15 mm apart across x = -0.03 to +0.03 and placed 50 mm ahead of the axle. That spacing keeps the tape covered by at least one sensor across the 25 mm line at most offsets, and the forward placement gives the controller a look-ahead before the wheels reach a bend. Weights are antisymmetric (-1, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 1), so a positive reading on the left side gives a positive signal, which steers left as the contract requires. Control: kp 3.0 keeps a moderate steering response (a signal of 0.5 gives about 525 PWM of differential). ki is 0 to avoid integral windup on bends. kd 0.05 adds light damping against the jitter that high kp can cause. Line loss uses last_direction so the robot searches toward the side it was last on. Geometry: a light 0.8 kg body with a 0.12 m wheel track gives quick yaw response, and a 0.12 m body width keeps the off-track limit at max(0.06, 0.0125 + 0.03) = 0.06 m. Expected result: completion on the development tracks with moderate rms error. The main risk is overshoot on the sharper slalom bends, which I will check in the critique.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.5,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.05,
    "sensor_weights": [-1.0, -0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor draft",
      "notes": "First draft with no prior telemetry: five forward-mounted sensors, moderate speed 1.5, kp 3 with light kd and last_direction line-loss recovery. Chosen from contract limits and physics reasoning; the critique should test the bend stability and speed trade-off."
    }
  }
}
